{% block content %}
  <main>
    <h1 class="section-title">The Science of Running</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      What does the research actually say about running? Here you'll find all the articles
      from the <strong>Science</strong> category in one place, written in plain language,
      without overclaiming, with the main scientific sources at the end of each article.
    </p>

    {% include "science-cards.njk" %}

    <div class="recap" style="margin-top:3rem;">
      <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"/><path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"/></svg>Where to start</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>1.</strong>&nbsp;<a href="post-vo2max-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">VO₂max</a>: the "engine" of your endurance.</li>
        <li><strong>2.</strong>&nbsp;<a href="post-lactate-threshold-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">Lactate threshold</a>: the threshold that sets your pace.</li>
        <li><strong>3.</strong>&nbsp;<a href="post-zones-palmon-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">Heart-rate zones</a>: how it all translates into heart rate.</li>
        <li><strong>4.</strong>&nbsp;<a href="post-easy-running-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">Easy running &amp; 80/20</a>: how elites actually train.</li>
        <li><strong>5.</strong>&nbsp;<a href="post-cadence-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">Cadence</a>: the technique side: steps and step length.</li>
        <li><strong>6.</strong>&nbsp;<a href="post-cardiac-drift-en.html" style="color:var(--accent);">Cardiac drift</a>: why heart rate climbs at the same pace.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top:4rem;">Tools that bring the theory to life</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Theory makes sense when you apply it to your own numbers.
    </p>
    <div class="cards cards-centered">
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 14c1.49-1.46 3-3.21 3-5.5A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 16.5 3c-1.76 0-3 .5-4.5 2-1.5-1.5-2.74-2-4.5-2A5.5 5.5 0 0 0 2 8.5c0 2.29 1.49 4.04 3 5.5l7 7Z"/></svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Heart-Rate Zones</h3>
        <p>
          Calculate your 5 personal training zones from your age, or with the Karvonen
          method if you also know your resting heart rate.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more" href="zones-palmon-en.html">Open the tool →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <div class="icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 6v6l4 2"/></svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h3>Pace Calculator</h3>
        <p>
          Enter a distance and a time to see your pace per kilometre, or the target time
